   "reply": "For an empty store, `list` prints nothing and exits with code 0. I ran it with `NOTES_HOME` pointed at a fresh temp directory:\n\n```\n$ NOTES_HOME=<empty dir> python -m fieldnotes.cli list\n$ echo $?\n0\n```\n\n`store.load()` returns `[]` when `notes.json` doesn't exist, so the loop in `cli.py` has nothing to print. `list` doesn't create the file either.\n\n`NOTES_HOME` isn't set in this shell. `store.notes_path()` reads `os.environ[\"NOTES_HOME\"]` directly, so running `list` without it raises a `KeyError`.\n\nI couldn't save the note about `NOTES_HOME` to the project. Writing `CLAUDE.md` was denied by your permission settings, so I haven't stored it anywhere. If you want it kept, allow writes to that file and I'll add it. You can also add this line yourself:\n\n> Notes are stored in `notes.json` under the directory named by the `NOTES_HOME` environment variable.",
